<InfoPage title="About us" description="Learn about Font Finder and our approach to making font discovery more practical." canonical="https://fontfinder.com/about-us" eyebrow="About Font Finder">
	<p class="text-lg leading-8 text-ink">Font Finder helps people turn a typographic reference into a useful next step.</p>
	<p>We built Font Finder for designers, marketers, developers, and curious type lovers who spot a great letterform in the wild and need to know where to begin. A screenshot, logo, poster, or product label can be the start of a more informed font choice.</p>
	<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-.04em] text-ink">Useful, not just accurate</h2><p class="mt-3">A font name alone is rarely enough. Our goal is to make the comparison practical: show likely matches, explain the visible characteristics, and surface free alternatives when an exact face is paid, custom, or unavailable.</p></section>
	<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-.04em] text-ink">Made for careful choices</h2><p class="mt-3">Typography carries meaning. We encourage you to compare the actual letterforms, test a candidate with your own words, and review the original license before using a font in published work. Font Finder is a guide for that decision—not a substitute for your own visual judgment.</p></section>
	<section class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-.04em] text-ink">Have a question?</h2><p class="mt-2">We’d be glad to hear from you.</p><a href="/contact-us" class="mt-4 inline-flex rounded-full bg-ink px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-black focus-visible:focus-ring">Contact us <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
</InfoPage>
